{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "6d820842-11dd-46a8-8511-1bbe42f2812f",
    "name": "simple-auth (Go)",
    "description": "REST API for the Go `simple-auth` project (Gin + GORM + PostgreSQL + JWT).\n\n## Quick start\n1. Start the API: `make db-up && make migrate-up && make dev`\n2. **Once:** run **01 Auth → Sign up admin account**, then promote it: `echo \"UPDATE users SET role = 'admin' WHERE email = 'admin@example.com';\" | make db-psql`\n3. Select the **simple-auth local** environment (top right).\n4. Run **01 Auth → Sign up**, **Log in** and **Log in as admin**. Both tokens are saved automatically.\n5. Every other request now works. Or run the whole collection with the **Runner** (top to bottom).\n\n## How auth works here\nAuth is set **once on the collection**: `Bearer {{accessToken}}` (the regular user). Requests inherit it. Admin-only requests override it with `Bearer {{adminToken}}`. Public requests (health, signup, login) are set to *No Auth*.\n\n## Variables\n- **Environment** (config you edit): `baseUrl`, `userName`, `userPassword`, `adminEmail`, `adminPassword`\n- **Collection variables** (filled by scripts while running): `userEmail`, `userId`, `accessToken`, `otherUserEmail`, `managedUserEmail`, `managedUserId`, `adminToken`, `adminId`\n\n## Error format\nEvery error is `{ \"error\": { \"code\", \"message\", \"fields\"? } }`. A collection-level test checks this on every 4xx/5xx response.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Runs after EVERY request in the collection",
          "pm.test(\"Responds in under 2 seconds\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.responseTime).to.be.below(2000));",
          "",
          "if (pm.response.code !== 204) {",
          "    pm.test(\"Response is JSON\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\")).to.include(\"application/json\"));",
          "}",
          "",
          "if (pm.response.code >= 400) {",
          "    pm.test(\"Error uses the standard shape { error: { code, message } }\", () => {",
          "        const err = pm.response.json().error;",
          "        pm.expect(err).to.have.property(\"code\");",
          "        pm.expect(err).to.have.property(\"message\");",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "description": "Fallback if no environment is selected"
    },
    {
      "key": "userName",
      "value": "Test User"
    },
    {
      "key": "userPassword",
      "value": "password123"
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Sign up"
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Sign up"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Log in"
    },
    {
      "key": "otherUserEmail",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Sign up – 'role: admin' is ignored"
    },
    {
      "key": "managedUserEmail",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Create user"
    },
    {
      "key": "managedUserId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Create user (admin)"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "admin@example.com",
      "description": "Admin account (promoted with SQL)"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "admin12345",
      "description": "Admin account (promoted with SQL)"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Log in as admin"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminId",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Set by Log in as admin (from the token)"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 Health",
      "description": "Is the API up and can it reach Postgres?",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
            "description": "Returns API and database status. Public.\n\n`503` means the API is running but cannot reach Postgres.",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"API and database are up\", () => {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(body.status).to.equal(\"ok\");",
                  "    pm.expect(body.database).to.equal(\"up\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "01 Auth",
      "description": "Sign up, log in and get the current user.\n\nRun **Sign up → Log in** first: they fill `userEmail`, `userId` and `accessToken` for every other request.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sign up",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup",
            "description": "Creates a **regular** user (role is always `user`). Public.\n\nThe pre-request script generates a unique email each run and stores it in `userEmail`, so you can run this repeatedly. The test script saves the new id in `userId`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"{{userName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// Unique email per run so signup never collides with an earlier run",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"userEmail\", `user.${Date.now()}@example.com`);"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "",
                  "const user = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Returns the new user with role 'user'\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(user.id).to.be.a(\"number\");",
                  "    pm.expect(user.email).to.equal(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"userEmail\").toLowerCase());",
                  "    pm.expect(user.role).to.equal(\"user\");",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"Never returns the password\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(user).to.not.have.property(\"password\");",
                  "    pm.expect(user).to.not.have.property(\"passwordHash\");",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"userId\", user.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
            "description": "Exchanges email + password for a JWT access token. Public.\n\nThe test script saves the token in `accessToken`. Every request that inherits auth from the collection then sends `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` automatically.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Returns a Bearer access token\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(body.tokenType).to.equal(\"Bearer\");",
                  "    pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a(\"string\");",
                  "    pm.expect(body.expiresIn).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"accessToken\", body.accessToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get current user (me)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
            "description": "Returns the logged-in user, read fresh from the database. Requires a token (inherited from the collection)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Returns the logged-in user\", () => {",
                  "    const me = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(me.id).to.equal(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"userId\")));",
                  "    pm.expect(me.email).to.equal(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"userEmail\").toLowerCase());",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Sign up admin account (one-time)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup",
            "description": "Creates the account for `adminEmail` (as a regular user, like any signup). Returns `409` on later runs because it already exists, which is fine.\n\n**Then, once, make it an admin in the database:**\n\n```bash\necho \"UPDATE users SET role = 'admin' WHERE email = 'admin@example.com';\" | make db-psql\n```",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Admin\",\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201 Created (first run) or 409 Conflict (already exists)\", () => pm.expect([201, 409]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Log in as admin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
            "description": "Logs in as `adminEmail` and saves the token in `adminToken`. Admin-only requests use this token.\n\nThe account must have `role = 'admin'` in the database (see *Sign up admin account*).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Returns an access token\", () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a(\"string\"));",
                  "",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminToken\", body.accessToken);",
                  "",
                  "// The token's payload (middle part) contains the admin's id as \"uid\"",
                  "const payload = JSON.parse(atob(body.accessToken.split(\".\")[1].replace(/-/g, \"+\").replace(/_/g, \"/\")));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminId\", payload.uid);",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Account has the admin role (if not: run the UPDATE from 'Sign up admin account')\", () => pm.expect(payload.role).to.equal(\"admin\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Negative cases",
          "description": "Requests that must fail. Each one checks the status code and the error `code`.",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "Sign up – duplicate email (409)",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup",
                "description": "Signing up again with `userEmail` must fail with `409 conflict`.",
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Duplicate\",\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test(\"409 Conflict\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                      "pm.test(\"Error code is 'conflict'\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.equal(\"conflict\"));"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Sign up – invalid body (400)",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup",
                "description": "Every field is invalid, so the response lists an error per field.",
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"J\",\n  \"email\": \"not-an-email\",\n  \"password\": \"short\"\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test(\"400 Bad Request\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                      "pm.test(\"Lists an error for each invalid field\", () => {",
                      "    const err = pm.response.json().error;",
                      "    pm.expect(err.code).to.equal(\"validation_failed\");",
                      "    pm.expect(err.fields).to.have.property(\"name\");",
                      "    pm.expect(err.fields).to.have.property(\"email\");",
                      "    pm.expect(err.fields).to.have.property(\"password\");",
                      "});"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Sign up – 'role: admin' is ignored",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/signup",
                "description": "Security check: sending `\"role\": \"admin\"` must still create a regular user. The email is saved in `otherUserEmail` and used later by *Update user – email taken*.",
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Sneaky\",\n  \"email\": \"{{otherUserEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\",\n  \"role\": \"admin\"\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "prerequest",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"otherUserEmail\", `other.${Date.now()}@example.com`);"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test(\"201 Created\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                      "pm.test(\"Role is still 'user'\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().role).to.equal(\"user\"));"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Log in – wrong password (401)",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
                "description": "Wrong password gives the same message as an unknown email, so attackers can't tell which emails exist.",
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong-password\"\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test(\"401 Unauthorized\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                      "pm.test(\"Generic message\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.message).to.equal(\"invalid email or password\"));"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Log in – unknown email (401)",
              "request": {
                "method": "POST",
                "header": [
                  {
                    "key": "Content-Type",
                    "value": "application/json"
                  }
                ],
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
                "description": "Same response as a wrong password.",
                "body": {
                  "mode": "raw",
                  "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"nobody@example.com\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\"\n}",
                  "options": {
                    "raw": {
                      "language": "json"
                    }
                  }
                },
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test(\"401 Unauthorized\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                      "pm.test(\"Generic message\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.message).to.equal(\"invalid email or password\"));"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Me – no token (401)",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
                "description": "No `Authorization` header at all.",
                "auth": {
                  "type": "noauth"
                }
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test(\"401 Unauthorized\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                      "pm.test(\"Error code is 'unauthorized'\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.equal(\"unauthorized\"));"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Me – invalid token (401)",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "header": [],
                "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/me",
                "description": "A token that was not signed by this API.",
                "auth": {
                  "type": "bearer",
                  "bearer": [
                    {
                      "key": "token",
                      "value": "not.a.valid-token",
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "type": "text/javascript",
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test(\"401 Unauthorized\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                      "pm.test(\"Says the token is invalid\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.message).to.equal(\"invalid or expired token\"));"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 Users",
      "description": "User management with access rules:\n\n| Action | Regular user | Admin |\n|---|---|---|\n| List / get | ✅ | ✅ |\n| Update profile | own only | anyone |\n| Create / delete / change role | ❌ 403 | ✅ |\n\nThe last admin can't be demoted or deleted (409).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List users",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users",
            "description": "Lists all users (soft-deleted users are hidden). **Any logged-in user.** Uses the regular user's token."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const users = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"Returns an array that includes the signed-up user\", () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(users).to.be.an(\"array\");",
                  "    const ids = users.map(u => u.id);",
                  "    pm.expect(ids).to.include(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"userId\")));",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test(\"No user exposes a password\", () => {",
                  "    users.forEach(u => {",
                  "        pm.expect(u).to.not.have.property(\"password\");",
                  "        pm.expect(u).to.not.have.property(\"passwordHash\");",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get user by id",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}",
            "description": "Gets one user. **Any logged-in user.**"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Returns the requested user\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.equal(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"userId\"))));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Update own profile",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{userId}}",
            "description": "A regular user updates **their own** profile. Only the fields you send change (name, email, password).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Updated Self\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200 OK\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Name changed, role unchanged\", () => {",
                  "    const user = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(user.name).to.equal(\"Updated Self\");",
                  "    pm.expect(user.role).to.equal(\"user\");",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create user (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users",
            "description": "Creates a user directly and can set `role`. **Admin only** (uses `adminToken`). Saves the id in `managedUserId`.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Managed User\",\n  \"email\": \"{{managedUserEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{userPassword}}\",\n  \"role\": \"user\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{adminToken}}",
